Package: kumarsurv
Title: Copula-Based Kumaraswamy Regression for Anomaly Detection in Doubly Bounded Time Series
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Raydonal", "Ospina", email = "raydonal@castlab.org", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9884-9090")),
    person("Jonatha S.", "Pimentel", email = "jonatha.sousa@ufpe.br", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2982-5383")),
    person("Francisco", "Cribari-Neto", email = "francisco.cribari@ufpe.br", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5909-6698"))
    )
Description: Maximum-likelihood estimation of a marginal regression model for time
    series in the unit interval, with a Kumaraswamy marginal distribution
    parametrized directly by a quantile of prescribed level, serial dependence
    induced by a Gaussian copula with ARMA structure, and an anomaly-detection
    layer (predictive quantile residuals, one-step prediction bands, a
    cumulative sum chart calibrated by average run length). Companion package
    to Ospina, Pimentel and Cribari-Neto, "Copula-Based Kumaraswamy Regression
    for Anomaly Detection in Doubly Bounded Time Series", reproducing every
    number, table and figure in the paper and its supplementary material from
    the scripts in inst/scripts/.
